ns\n- per-input validation / verification state\n- per-record materialization fields\n\nFrozen Don Delta precedent also binds full consumed content through statePayload.inputs.\n\n────────────────────────────\nOBJECTIVE\n────────────────────────────\n\nRepair materialization identity so every input field capable of changing materialized output is hash-load-bearing.\n\nDo NOT redesign the layer.\nDo NOT change suppression semantics.\nDo NOT change FixedDec6dp behavior.\nDo NOT change lane legality.\nDo NOT change roundHalfUpMicro.\nDo NOT change selection/event scope rules.\nDo NOT modify unrelated contracts.\n\n────────────────────────────\nREQUIRED HASH STATE\n────────────────────────────\n\nThe canonical materialization state payload must bind, at minimum:\n\n1. Materialization contract/version\n2. Input assertion identity\n3. Input assertion version\n4. Don-declared variable\n5. Don-declared lane\n6. Signed FixedDec6dp magnitude\n7. Input validation state\n8. Input verification state\n9. Any suppression-relevant status\n10. Any baseline/proxy state that changes materialization behavior\n11. Per-record fields used to produce the executable valueSurface\n12. Deterministic ordering information necessary to make the payload canonical\n\nThe rule is:\n\nIF changing a field can change:\n- inclusion/exclusion\n- suppression\n- executable magnitude\n- lane\n- record identity\n- record semantics\n- downstream valueSurface\n\nTHEN that field must be represented in canonical hash state.\n\nDo not hash only assertionId references.\n\n────────────────────────────\nCANONICALIZATION\n────────────────────────────\n\nUse one deterministic canonical serialization path.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- stable field ordering\n- stable record ordering\n- FixedDec6dp remains integer micro-units\n- no float serialization\n- no clock/timestamp entropy\n- no machine/path entropy\n- no mutable runtime metadata\n- no redundant second hash primitive\n\nPreserve the existing single hash primitive.\n\n─