ssion cleanup decisions.\n\nThat did **not** require architecture work.\n\nThe later live MLB slate workflow — Falcon freeze → experimental engine → inspect results — was a **normal operational run**, not an architecture change.\n\nOnly after the engine exposed genuine methodology defects did some deeper work become justified, specifically:\n\n- run-line probability was not actually a cover model,\n- totals μ was compressed,\n- juice-gate state handling was defective,\n- schema aliasing existed.\n\nEven then, the correct scope was still a bounded methodology/implementation correction inside the experimental MLB lane.\n\n---\n\n# C. ACTUAL WORK PERFORMED\n\nOnly concrete work that was actually reported as built, changed, verified, or produced is included here.\n\n### MLB cleanup / recon\n\nThe session began from a completed estate recon:\n\n- 506-file estate inventoried and hash-verified.\n- 11 recon deliverables produced.\n- 50 exact-duplicate groups identified.\n- 71 lineage families identified.\n- 12 supersession chains identified.\n- 4 quarantine candidates identified.\n- 0 delete candidates identified.\n- Identity anomalies and schema gaps documented.\n- `float(IP)` defects identified.\n- generic `(\"OUT\",\"IL\")` counting identified.\n- triple-run identical-output anomaly identified.\n- cleanup decision register prepared.\n\n### 2026-09-24 MLB live experimental run\n\nFalcon produced a real pregame frozen evidence package:\n\n- 12/12 games collected.\n- markets present across five books; Bet365/Circa gaps explicitly accepted.\n- 72 odds rows.\n- starters 23/24.\n- bullpen 24/24 with 450 relievers.\n- injuries and roster data collected.\n- weather 12/12.\n- frozen snapshot `20260924_151712`.\n- regression scripts passed.\n- prior day artifacts untouched.\n\nThat was a **visible, runnable milestone**.\n\nThe experimental engine then actually ran against the frozen package:\n\n- 11/12 games analyzed.\n- MIL@PHI failed closed.\n- full market grid produced.\n- six original ML review rows surfaced.\n- 14 reported ≥7% conflict rows surfaced.\n- negative-EV rows retained.\n- odds-consumption perturbation test proved BetMGM prices were actually consumed.\n\nThis was another **visible outcome**.\n\n### Kimi corrective work\n\nConcrete defects were found and corrected:\n\n- run-line lane confirmed to lack a real margin/cover model.\n- run-line candidate path failed closed.\n- juice-gate dual-accounting defect fixed with one authoritative `final_state`.\n- `total`/`totals` schema drift normalized at ingestion.\n- totals compression diagnosed but deliberately not recalibrated.\n- replay produced:\n  - 0 candidates,\n  - 4 reviews,\n  - 30 methodology conflicts,\n  - 3 data-insufficient.\n- 166/166 or equivalent corrective suite state was later reported in a separate branch.\n- frozen data remained unchanged.\n\n### Luce verification of r7\n\nLuce independently confirmed:\n\n- run-line root cause,\n- totals compression diagnosis,\n- juice-gate defect and fix,\n- schema normalization,\n- replay counts,\n- frozen evidence integrity,\n- odds consumption.\n\nThis was legitimate verification and produced a useful acceptance boundary.\n\n### Totals methodology research\n\nKimi later produced a real research result:\n\n- 14 scored games were usable.\n- no training/validation split was fabricated.\n- 0/0/14 train/validation/holdout was explicitly reported.\n- coefficient scaling and F5 functional form were identified as likely causes.\n- no totals fit was performed.\n- no totals candidate promotion occurred.\n\nThat was valid research, but not a completed calibration.\n\n### Separate ECQ / DevPad work\n\nLater in the chat, unrelated work was introduced and genuinely performed:\n\n- ECQ materialization FIX 1 hash-integrity defect was found.\n- Nico implemented a fix binding assertion content and record content into identity.\n- 166/166 tests reportedly passed.\n- Chiave ruled on envelope versioning.\n- Nico implemented canonical transform and 